70
00:31:39,042 --> 00:32:04,253
So again, you can see that these buildings are one and two stories tall. I think the tallest is 28 feet. They take up most of the lots either in building or parking lot. And the only real green or pervious space to water is here at Winterbrook for the most part.

71
00:32:06,886 --> 00:32:31,473
Regionally, if we're looking at the site here in the center of the screen, we have a fairly well-developed bike path on this side around the Mystic River and up the Mystic River. I understand from staff here that people use the underpass here on 93 and come up Mystic Gap. We'd like to continue to encourage that.

72
00:32:31,895 --> 00:33:01,662
We're proposing a multi-use path bike and pedestrian around the entire site on the 93 side and the south here by the car dealership so that you can bypass if you're on a bicycle or walking, running, you can bypass the kind of busy intersection here. The 95 bus running up and down route to Mystic Ave

73
00:33:02,303 --> 00:33:27,346
At this point, there are two stops on our side and two stops on the other side, north and southbound. Location of the Green Line extension and Orange Line. You can see that the site is pretty well located. You can see Boston here in the background in 93,

74
00:33:27,599 --> 00:33:53,941
and 38 here. So it seems to be in our minds, at least ripe for redevelopment. So Chris had talked a little bit about kind of a critical mass or the ability to attract a large tenant who needs a fair amount of space.

75
00:33:54,565 --> 00:34:17,633
We've looked at ways to do that it is a large site, but it's not incredibly large. So, we are suggesting some changes from the original C to zoning the C to zoning is listed on the left here. And again that's restricted to one or two story buildings and 35 feet in height.

76
00:34:18,410 --> 00:34:47,452
At this point, there is a maximum lot coverage of 50% and no real west depth or open space or landscape space requirements at this point. Our new development, we were proposed to keep all the original C2 zoning uses, which are still largely commercial.

77
00:34:48,211 --> 00:35:13,338
And we'd like to change research and testing laboratory, which is what a research and development lab would be classified under in the city, from an appeal, Board of Appeals appeal, to an allowed use, and that'd be part of the district. The lot area frontage lot width

